1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,350
<font color="#000000">Neuroformer is a multimodal,</font>

2
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:06,416
<font color="#000000">multitask generative pretrained transformer for
brain data,</font>

3
00:00:06,496 --> 00:00:08,207
<font color="#000000">built at UC Santa Barbara.</font>

4
00:00:08,287 --> 00:00:14,479
<font color="#000000">It reframes cellular-resolution spike analysis as
autoregressive spatiotemporal generation,</font>

5
00:00:14,559 --> 00:00:18,682
<font color="#000000">borrowing the recipe behind large language and
vision models.</font>

6
00:00:18,762 --> 00:00:24,540
<font color="#000000">Trained self-supervised, it recovers circuit
connectivity and decodes mouse behavior.</font>

7
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:29,685
<font color="#000000">Modern neuroscience records thousands of neurons at
cellular resolution,</font>

8
00:00:29,765 --> 00:00:32,243
<font color="#000000">alongside visual stimuli and behavior.</font>

9
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:35,473
<font color="#000000">These datasets are large, multimodal, and messy,</font>

10
00:00:35,553 --> 00:00:40,386
<font color="#000000">yet the field's traditional statistical tools were
built for far smaller,</font>

11
00:00:40,466 --> 00:00:44,760
<font color="#000000">single-modality recordings, leaving a widening
data-analysis gap.</font>

12
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:50,549
<font color="#000000">Large pretrained models in vision and language
point a way forward: they learn general</font>

13
00:00:50,629 --> 00:00:53,485
<font color="#000000">representations self-supervised from raw data,</font>

14
00:00:53,565 --> 00:00:55,719
<font color="#000000">then transfer with little labeling.</font>

15
00:00:55,799 --> 00:01:01,655
<font color="#000000">The authors ask whether reframing spike analysis as
generative prediction can likewise scale,</font>

16
00:01:01,735 --> 00:01:04,910
<font color="#000000">fuse modalities, and transfer to behavior decoding.</font>

17
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:07,957
<font color="#000000">Neuroformer makes four contributions.</font>

18
00:01:08,037 --> 00:01:13,303
<font color="#000000">It reframes spike analysis as self-supervised
autoregressive generation,</font>

19
00:01:13,383 --> 00:01:14,640
<font color="#000000">needing no labels.</font>

20
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:20,580
<font color="#000000">Its cross-attention scales linearly with feature
size and fuses many modalities.</font>

21
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:25,629
<font color="#000000">On simulated data, its attention maps recover
directed connectivity,</font>

22
00:01:25,709 --> 00:01:28,673
<font color="#000000">including hub neurons correlation misses.</font>

23
00:01:28,753 --> 00:01:32,980
<font color="#000000">Pretrained, it decodes behavior with few-shot fine-tuning.</font>

24
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:36,246
<font color="#000000">Neuroformer treats each spike as a token,</font>

25
00:01:36,326 --> 00:01:39,717
<font color="#000000">splitting activity into Current and Past States.</font>

26
00:01:39,797 --> 00:01:43,551
<font color="#000000">Video becomes patches via a 3D-convolutional encoder;</font>

27
00:01:43,631 --> 00:01:45,938
<font color="#000000">behavior forms a separate stream.</font>

28
00:01:46,018 --> 00:01:50,856
<font color="#000000">A contrastive module aligns neural, visual, and
behavioral features.</font>

29
00:01:50,936 --> 00:01:55,703
<font color="#000000">Cross-attention fuses the Current State with larger
feature arrays,</font>

30
00:01:55,783 --> 00:01:59,174
<font color="#000000">cutting attention cost from quadratic to linear.</font>

31
00:01:59,254 --> 00:02:04,310
<font color="#000000">A causally masked decoder predicts which neuron
fires and its time bin.</font>

32
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:08,083
<font color="#000000">Validation spans two levels.</font>

33
00:02:08,163 --> 00:02:11,556
<font color="#000000">First,</font>

34
00:02:11,636 --> 00:02:15,029
<font color="#000000">a simulated spiking network with three hub neurons
gives a ground-truth connectivity matrix.</font>

35
00:02:15,109 --> 00:02:18,501
<font color="#000000">Second,</font>

36
00:02:18,581 --> 00:02:21,974
<font color="#000000">two-photon calcium imaging of mouse visual cortex
records 386 neurons across V1 and AL</font>

37
00:02:22,054 --> 00:02:25,447
<font color="#000000">viewing gratings and natural videos,</font>

38
00:02:25,527 --> 00:02:28,920
<font color="#000000">plus a virtual-navigation dataset pairing activity
with running speed.</font>

39
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:31,097
<font color="#000000">On the simulated network,</font>

40
00:02:31,177 --> 00:02:37,477
<font color="#000000">Neuroformer's attention reveals directed
connectivity and identifies the hub neurons,</font>

41
00:02:37,557 --> 00:02:41,831
<font color="#000000">which plain correlation misses for lack of directionality.</font>

42
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:47,161
<font color="#000000">On real cortex, it reproduces responses to gratings
and natural videos,</font>

43
00:02:47,241 --> 00:02:52,490
<font color="#000000">with population predictions significantly beating a
GLM, p around 0.02.</font>

44
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:57,970
<font color="#000000">Fine-tuned to decode running, it reaches Pearson
correlations up to 0.97.</font>

45
00:02:58,350 --> 00:03:03,413
<font color="#000000">An ablation removes components one at a time: the
Current State, Past State,</font>

46
00:03:03,493 --> 00:03:05,443
<font color="#000000">video stream, behavior stream,</font>

47
00:03:05,523 --> 00:03:09,706
<font color="#000000">and contrastive objective each add measurable
predictive power.</font>

48
00:03:09,786 --> 00:03:11,263
<font color="#000000">Two findings stand out.</font>

49
00:03:11,343 --> 00:03:15,932
<font color="#000000">Jointly training on neural responses and behavior
beats either alone,</font>

50
00:03:16,012 --> 00:03:20,060
<font color="#000000">and the contrastive objective helps most when data
is scarce.</font>

51
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:26,946
<font color="#FFFFFF">For behavior prediction, Neuroformer reaches
Pearson correlation up to 0.97,</font>

52
00:03:27,026 --> 00:03:29,372
<font color="#FFFFFF">versus about 0.73 for Lasso.</font>

53
00:03:29,452 --> 00:03:36,478
<font color="#FFFFFF">Few-shot, a model pretrained and fine-tuned on just
1% of behavior data hits 0.51,</font>

54
00:03:36,558 --> 00:03:42,197
<font color="#FFFFFF">beating a non-pretrained model given 10%, which
reaches only 0.33.</font>

55
00:03:42,277 --> 00:03:47,310
<font color="#FFFFFF">Its largest models scale to roughly 100 million
parameters.</font>

56
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:54,081
<font color="#000000">The takeaway: the pretraining paradigm that
reshaped vision and language can also work for the brain.</font>

57
00:03:54,161 --> 00:03:57,669
<font color="#000000">Treating spikes as autoregressive multimodal generation,</font>

58
00:03:57,749 --> 00:04:04,972
<font color="#000000">one self-supervised transformer recovers a
circuit's directed connectivity and decodes behavior from few examples,</font>

59
00:04:05,052 --> 00:04:08,560
<font color="#000000">pointing toward scalable neuroscience foundation models.</font>
